From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/rocket: reset the cores this SoC acquired

rocket_core_init() takes the reset bulk with soc->num_resets, one on
RK3576 and two on RK3588, but rocket_core_reset() still walks
ARRAY_SIZE(core->resets).  On RK3576 that asserts and deasserts an entry
nothing acquired.

Nothing has gone wrong so far because struct rocket_core is kzalloc'd
and the reset core accepts a NULL rstc, so the extra entry is a pair of
no-ops.  It stops being harmless the moment the missing reset is real:
srst_h is not absent on RK3576, it is driven from the NPU power domain,
so a reset here that silently covers one of two lines and a reset that
covers one of one read the same in the code and differ on the hardware.

Use the count the resets were acquired with.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.c
index 9b4cf979e..86654521c 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.c
@@ -149,9 +149,14 @@ void rocket_core_fini(struct rocket_core *core)
 
 void rocket_core_reset(struct rocket_core *core)
 {
-	reset_control_bulk_assert(ARRAY_SIZE(core->resets), core->resets);
+	/*
+	 * The same array rocket_core_init() acquired, so the same count: walking
+	 * ARRAY_SIZE() here reaches an entry no SoC asked for, which on RK3576 is
+	 * the srst_h its power domain drives instead.
+	 */
+	reset_control_bulk_assert(core->soc->num_resets, core->resets);
 
 	udelay(10);
 
-	reset_control_bulk_deassert(ARRAY_SIZE(core->resets), core->resets);
+	reset_control_bulk_deassert(core->soc->num_resets, core->resets);
 }
